[2026/07/09 01:42:24] [DEBUG] isgsa.nodeAgent: Review summary: ## Bug/Issue Summary

The experiment encountered a **timeout failure** during the Amazon2014VideoGames dataset processing. Specifically, the execution was terminated with `TimeoutError: Execution exceeded the time limit of an hour` during the Predict phase of PopScorer for the last dataset.

### Root Cause
The Amazon2014VideoGames dataset contains ~1.3M interactions, making it computationally expensive when running ALS (ImplicitMFScorer - which requires iterative optimization) and ItemKNN (which computes pairwise item similarities) across 5 different random seeds. The total execution time exceeded the 1-hour limit imposed by the runtime environment.

### Impact
